Fix for mt76-vendor 'dump csi' SIGSEGV.
Base: mediatek/mtk-openwrt-feeds @ a15454c888f4f4144c50e33b5feef4f247c5f78b
  feed/app/mt76-vendor/src/csi.c

Root cause: the driver seeds its per-dump counter on the FIRST dumpit
callback and only then decrements it, so a request for CSI_DUMP_PER_NUM=3
yields FOUR records. Userspace sized csi[] for pkt_num but looped pkt_num/3
times, storing up to 4*(pkt_num/3) records with no bounds check, so any dump
with >= pkt_num records buffered wrote past the allocation. A dump that found
only one record buffered never overran, which is why the single association
record succeeded and every data-frame dump crashed.

Also fixed: the JSON writer passed the full MAX_BUF_SIZE to every snprintf
instead of the remaining space, and three attributes were dereferenced without
being in the presence check.
